  "executive_briefing": "The 2026 global tax landscape is defined by the crystallization of the OECD Pillar Two framework as a core compliance pillar for multinational enterprises. While large economies navigate the operational complexities of a 15% global minimum tax, there is a visible pivot toward fiscal precision. Jurisdictions like Singapore and other ASEAN members are emphasizing targeted, innovation-linked incentives over broad-based rate reductions to sustain FDI in this new environment. Concurrently, the global trade environment remains highly volatile, with unilateral tariff measures and shifting supply chain strategies compelling firms to prioritize agility. Real-time digital tax administration, particularly e-invoicing, has moved beyond pilot phases into mandatory enforcement, fundamentally reshaping audit and compliance architectures.",
